This directory holds the cpo's drift audit log — a compact record of past
verdicts (item / risk / confidence / register / outcome) so the operator (or a
review) can verify the cpo hasn't quietly reclassified dangerous items as
routine over time. See MEMORY.md §drift audit and EVALUATION.md §failure modes.

One file per audit slice, named `YYYY-MM-DD-<slug>.md`. Append-only by nature
(past verdicts are evidence). Compact: one row per verdict, not full reasoning.

This `.keep` file marks the directory as operator-owned at the manifest layer:
swarm-init seeds it once; sync and --force never touch it.
